      tech_short: 'tech_short',
      features_long:
        '<p>As a dedicated software engineer, I undertook the exhilarating challenge of developing a <u>SAAS</u> web application that fosters a vibrant community of photographers. This innovative platform not only facilitates seamless photo uploads but also empowers <u>photographers </u>to engage in contests, receive user feedback, and share their work on social media. My responsibilities encompassed the creation of both client and admin <u>dashboards</u>, demonstrating my versatile skill set. Leveraging an extensive array of technologies, including <u>React</u>, <u>Node.js</u>, <u>Bootstrap</u>, <u>jQuery</u>, <u>HTML</u>, <u>CSS</u>, <u>MongoDB</u>, <u>Docker</u>, <u>CI/CD</u>, <u>AWS</u>, and various <u>social media APIs</u>, I contributed to building a thriving and interactive photography ecosystem.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2><strong>Key Modules and Contributions:</strong></h2><p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong>Photographer Community Platform:</strong><br>At the heart of this SAAS application lies a robust platform that brings photographers together. I architected modules that enable seamless photo uploads, categorization, and interaction with user-generated content.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong>Contests and Engagement Features:</strong><br>I designed and implemented the contest module, allowing photographers to participate, while users could upvote, comment, and share the submitted photos on social media. This module emphasizes my expertise in fostering user engagement.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong>Client and Admin Dashboards (React, Bootstrap):</strong><br>I meticulously developed intuitive client and admin dashboards. The client dashboard allows photographers to manage their portfolios, participate in contests, and engage with their audience. The admin dashboard empowers administrators to curate contests, moderate content, and manage user interactions.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong>&nbsp;Backend Architecture (Node.js, MongoDB, Mongoose):</strong><br>My responsibilities extended to crafting a resilient backend architecture using Node.js. MongoDB and Mongoose served as the backbone for efficient data storage, retrieval, and management. This backend module showcases my proficiency in server-side development and database design.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong>&nbsp;Database Design and Integration (MongoDB, Amazon RDS):</strong><br>I took charge of designing MongoDB schemas for the core application, as well as integrating Amazon RDS for more complex data requirements. This highlights my adaptability in working with different database systems.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong>Deployment and CI/CD (Docker, GitHub Actions):</strong><br>Recognizing the significance of efficient deployment, I containerized the application using Docker. CI/CD pipelines were set up using GitHub Actions, ensuring a streamlined workflow from development to production.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong>Social Media Integration (APIs):</strong><br>I integrated various social media APIs, enabling photographers to seamlessly share their work across different platforms. This demonstrates my ability to work with external APIs for enhanced functionality.&nbsp;</li></ul><h2><br><strong>My Responsibilities:&nbsp;</strong></h2><p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong>Full-Stack Development:</strong> I undertook a comprehensive role, creating both the frontend and backend components of the SAAS application.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Dashboard Design:</strong> I crafted intuitive client and admin dashboards, using React and Bootstrap to ensure a user-friendly experience.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Engagement and Contests:</strong> I designed the contest module, fostering user engagement through voting, commenting, and sharing.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Database Management:</strong> I designed MongoDB schemas and integrated Amazon RDS, ensuring optimized data storage and retrieval.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Deployment and CI/CD:</strong> I containerized the application with Docker and established CI/CD pipelines using GitHub Actions for seamless deployment.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Social Media Integration:</strong> I integrated social media APIs, enabling photographers to share their work across multiple platforms.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><h2><strong>Tech Stack:&nbsp;</strong></h2><p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><span style="background-color:transparent;color:#000000;"><strong>&nbsp;Frontend: </strong>React, Bootstrap, jQuery, HTML, CSS</span></li><li><span style="background-color:transparent;color:#000000;"><strong>&nbsp;Backend: </strong>Node.js, MongoDB, Mongoose</span></li><li><span style="background-color:transparent;color:#000000;"><strong>&nbsp;Client and Admin Dashboards: </strong>Development and Design</span></li><li><span style="background-color:transparent;color:#000000;"><strong>&nbsp;Contests and Engagement: </strong>Voting, Comments, Sharing</span></li><li><span style="background-color:transparent;color:#000000;"><strong>&nbsp;Deployment: </strong>Docker, CI/CD (GitHub Actions), Amazon EC2</span></li><li><span style="background-color:transparent;color:#000000;"><strong>&nbsp;Database: </strong>MongoDB, Amazon RDS</span></li><li><span style="background-color:transparent;color:#000000;"><strong>&nbsp;Social Media: </strong>Various Social Media APIs</span></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Through my contributions to this SAAS web application, I have demonstrated my ability to craft a comprehensive and engaging platform that brings photographers together, fosters user engagement, and promotes sharing and learning within the photography community. By building client and admin dashboards, integrating social media, and orchestrating seamless deployment, I have contributed to a thriving ecosystem for photographers to showcase their work and connect with their audience.</p>',
